sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-dugesia-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dugesia-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dugesia-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Saturated Schnakenberg Turing wavelength for Dugesia japonica dorsal pigment at 6.912 µm (Holocene, Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 88.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the same kinetics and the same 6.912 µm linear wavelength. The saturated steady field peaks at Fourier mode 6, λ = 8.064 µm, which is reported beside λ_c rather than tuned away. Diffusion ratio R from 36 to 120 shortens λ monotonically, and equal diffusion (R = 1) has max σ = -0.565. Interior gray KS distance against the Nogi plate is D = 0.434 (reference null 0.5). The Kalininsky wild-type voucher yields two bodies with mean circularity 0.307. Linear dispersion Pearson r remains 0.99998. Overall 88.5/100 (faithfulness 88.0, reproducibility 89.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 80fe3e3968850cd5826acf65ba6a24cab2e95424; environment: python 3.12, lean not installed in this VM; theorems are Lean 4 prelude, unchecked here. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/dugesia_japonica_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-dugesia-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 80fe3e3968850cd5826acf65ba6a24cab2e95424, image/png, 458681 B, 1496×946 px, artifact_sha256 e752de071e812756f45c141918d762639cd72f07c5131a6f63bb267d0c7fdfff (sha256 e752de071e812756f45c141918d762639cd72f07c5131a6f63bb267d0c7fdfff), spec_fingerprint 69b07407b41111e3df409d09d284c8ed47d97c6e78075bf3f4f35e0a79d838da. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 69b07407b41111e3df409d09d284c8ed47d97c6e78075bf3f4f35e0a79d838da; artifact_sha256: e752de071e812756f45c141918d762639cd72f07c5131a6f63bb267d0c7fdfff; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/dugesia_japonica_turing_wavelength_s0/dugesia_japonica_field_kalininsky_ccby4.jpg=e40acb76c9286a8d..., datasets/dugesia_japonica_turing_wavelength_s0/dugesia_japonica_ocellus_pigment_nogi2009.png=6abf2ae940aa3115..., datasets/dugesia_japonica_turing_wavelength_s0/dugesia_japonica_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=2bc1220e0880d8c0...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-dugesia-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) gives the diffusion-driven instability and the critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg (1979), Gierer & Meinhardt (1972), and Murray (1981) supply the kinetics and the pigment-prepattern reading. | Nogi et al. (2009) published the CC BY 2.5 regenerated Dugesia japonica plate. Kalininsky's iNaturalist photo 226612281 is CC BY 4.0.; reconstructed_in_script: κ = 0.15, R = 48, D_u solved for λ_c = 6.912 µm, spectral integrator, seed 3213. | Nonlinear radial-FFT wavelength, KS interior comparison, diffusion-ratio sweep, and equal-diffusion ablation. | Pale-body segmentation of the wild-type voucher.; transfer_boundary: Kondo (2009) is a fish pigment wave. Lapan & Reddien (2012) is Schmidtea eye regeneration. Herath & Lobo (2020) is planarian fission, not this wavelength. | Neither specimen plate is a calibrated 6.912 µm micrograph.; does_not_claim: Does not claim 6.912 µm was measured on this species. It is the slot's detail-scale operating point (6.912e-6 m, log10 = -5.160), age 0 Ma. | Does not claim a fossil predecessor. Chronoseries 1/1. | Does not claim the brightness mask separates every worm on the Nogi plate.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Still one assessor. A second model has not scored this audit.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'The Nogi brightness mask still merges some adjacent animals. A watershed split was not required for the image-fitness gate and was not added.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.885"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; Pass 2)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

